+This node owns visit persistence, whole-visit revision tracking, and the rules that determine when a visit has a single usable current state versus unresolved competing revisions. A visit is identified by a client-generated UUID and references a plot UUID from `site-catalog`. Tablets may submit edits days after fetching a visit, so server receipt order is never treated as evidence that one worker's observations supersede another's.
 
